       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum for a supervised adult, which is 3,200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common dose for inflammatory conditions\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day total), a common analgesic dose\n- **1600 mg/day total**, if that was the daily figure you had in mind, which would be 400 mg four times daily\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it now."
